Z||000000||FieroLisa||05-21-2001||07:45 PM||||Well, Good.<P>I gave my '94 Mercury Tracer to my mom to take home to North Carolina so at the end of the year I wouldn't have 2 cars to drive home. She left it overnight in the airport parking garage while she had a business appointment. <P>Some @$$HOLE broke into it!!! why the HELL do you break into a crappy Tracer??<P>They broke the back window, stole my Panasonic CD Player (which is hilarious since the thing barely works since its 5 years old), Stole about 100 CDs and the 2 Factory Speakers in the back. Overall, about $2,000 worth of stuff stolen. In an airport garage. <P>Note to Self: Put alarm system in Fiero and keep it covered so no one can see whats in it.<P>I am SOOOOOO MAD right now.<P>This is the second car I've had someone break into, the coupe was first. <P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT: 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air intake<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>       <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48495967&Sequence=0&res=high"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||LZeitgeist||05-21-2001||08:17 PM||||Ohhhhhh, sh*t......... <P>God, airport parking garages are *so* f'ed up...... didn't they have security cameras???<P><BR>Arrrgh... sorry to hear that, Lisa...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||05-21-2001||08:37 PM||||When my first car was broken into and a $2,500 set of golf clubs were stolen, my mom used homeowners insurance to recoupe the money.  I know it sounds funny but it worked.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||05-21-2001||08:42 PM||||Damn Lisa. Sorry to hear that. (sidenote=that was a removable face radio, and you do tend to just leave all your stuff just laying on seats) Just keep your stuff hidden in the Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000004||kslish||05-21-2001||08:52 PM||||God Lisa, you have sure have bad luck when it comes to getting your cars broken into (not to mention your experiences with mechanics).  <P>Was this in Columbus or N. Carolina?<P>Unfortunately, there is no real sure-fire way to prevent this crap from happening.  If some jerk is going to be an @ss and do this, they are going to do it, or still cause damage in some way if they can't.  I had my Fiero keyed (causing $400 in paint damage) when my alarm went off when someone tried to get into it.  I installed the alarm in response to my Dad's immaculate '86 coupe with 32,000 miles being stolen a while back.  He just had "the Club" on it.  What really pissed us off was that they left the Club on the ground where the car was parked.  Kind of like they were taunting the owner for trying to protect the car.  The car was recovered a week later with $1200 worth of damage.  I feel your pain because the feeling one has when somthing like this happens absolutely sucks.....<P>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Sootah||05-21-2001||09:03 PM||||I honestly can't imagine how you feel, I had my CD player stolen out of my car about 1 1/2 years back and I went into a freaking rage; And this was a crappy Clarion, there were no CD's in the car at the time, and nothing else of value. I don't think that I have ever sworn that much. If I ever find out who did it I swear I am gonna break all of their windows and then their knees. **** .. Got myself riled up. Gonna go vent now, hopefully you can stay more level-headed then I can about <B>crap</B> like this...<P>------------------<BR>Never argue with an idiot, they drag you down to their level and then beat you with experience||||reg||8
Z||000006||Galen||05-21-2001||10:01 PM||||turn into KillerLisa... ravage everyone then calm down, and conduct yourself in a orderly fashion. find the culprit and string em up by the genitalia..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> if thats spelled right<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe Auto 4Banger - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR>AIM: WookieeNC||||reg||1
Z||000007||Taijiguy||05-21-2001||10:07 PM||||That sucks Lisa.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <BR>I don't lock my car any more. It's an exercise in futility. I arm the alarm, and leave the doors unlocked. I take the faceplate from my stereo with me, or lock stuff in the trunk. If they want in, they're gonna get in, it's unavoidable. I just hope my countermeasures are effective in preventing the car from being stolen if it comes to that. I had a car stolen once. Fortunately I got it back, they stole the speakers and my music, but I had outsmarted them in the stereo install, and they couldn't figure how to get it out.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> (obviously you don't have to be very bright to be a thief....a cowardly sneak thief at that)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroLisa||05-21-2001||10:23 PM||||UG I just hate people right now. I'm so scared for the Fiero mostly... What I plan on doing is getting an alarm which has a keychain that tells you when the car is armed and also alerts you when someone messes with it. That way if I'm not right near it and can't hear it, I can still know whats going off. <P>I'm also getting 2 different sets of locks for my wheels...<P>I might be getting too paranoid, but Now that I've had 2 cars broken into, each time over $1500 worth of stuff taken, I need to do something!<P>Roger: Well I was planning on taking that face plate off the Tracer but then realized my mom wouldnt know how to put it back on when she went to drive it back home. My CDs were buried under the ton of useless crap in my backseat. I also had 2 nice dresses and a bunch of other random crap from my dorm that they didn't take.<P>And why the hell did they take factory 6x9s, the market can't be good for that!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||fiero56||05-21-2001||10:37 PM||||I'll shut up. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 05-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||loafer87gt||05-22-2001||12:56 AM||||Sorry to hear about the bad news. Like Jeff said, it should be covered under your house insurance though. From my past break in experiences (had my GT broken into three times), your car insurance will cover all the stuff physically attached to the vehicle, like speakers and your headunit. Stuff like CD's, or valuables are covered under your house insurance. I live three hundred miles away from my parents, and I was still able to get all 100 of my CD's replaced under their house package. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Formula88||05-22-2001||02:14 AM||||I feel your pain, Lisa.  My 72 Trans Am was broken into one time to steal the radio - and that was in my carport!  Worst of all wasn't them stealing the radio, but the hack job they did on my console and dashboard trying to get it out.  They didn't even manage to get the head unit out and still destroyed my interior.  That was many years ago, and to this day, if I ever find out who did it.....||||reg||8
Z||000012||cscougar||05-22-2001||05:28 PM||||I tell people to just remember the theft if you ever get on a jury.... Put the criminals away for good... <P>This society is way too lenient on alot of crime and those burglaries illustrate that.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Jake_Dragon||05-22-2001||05:31 PM||||Mousetrap with a razor blade soldered on it.<BR>Be careful when you set it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Friend of mine actually found this setup in a car he just bought, rusty blade as well!<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/rebel33/logo.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||JSocha||05-22-2001||05:41 PM||||About two/three years ago, my step daughter Wendy parked my wife's 97 Dodge 1500 on a street she shouldn't have (this in a town of less then 3,000 people mind you).<P>Somebody broke the back window on the passenger side, scratched the paint (as well on the drivers side tryin to get into that window) and took my wife's Motorola Bag Cell Phone I bought for her.<P>Stupid thing is, they are worthless if stolen and the ESN number is reported and they had been preaching that for many months here in town as the crime rate went up when a Pawn shop decided to locate here in town.  <P>The one we had needed a 4 digit PIN code to unlock it to do anything.  Never recovered it and somebody probably still has a useless bag phone probably sitting in their closet now, thinking one day they will activate it and yet the ESN number is in a database of stolen cell phones.  I hope they do!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||thomas_l||05-22-2001||05:55 PM||||Now to go completely off topic  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Jake - nice idea about the mousetraps. You just need to figure out what to do when the police come after <I>you</I> for setting a "mantrap". Your post reminded me of a story about a rural Georgia convenience store owner that got tired of someone ripping off his Coke machine at night. So he rigged the thing with some dynamite in such a way that normal purchasers would be unharmed but a thief would get a surprise. The theif got his arm blown off that night, but he now owns the store thanks to the wrongful injury suit he won after the criminal trial...||||reg||10
